<Layout title="Terms of Use | Math Worksheet Studio" description="Terms for using free browser-generated math practice sheets, PDFs and answer keys from Math Worksheet Studio." canonicalPath="/terms/">
 <div class="container"><article class="simple-copy">
  <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
  <p><strong>Last updated: November 7, 2026.</strong> Math Worksheet Studio provides free printable mathematics practice materials and matching answers for teachers, parents, tutors and independent learners.</p>
  <h2>Educational use</h2>
  <p>You may generate, download and print worksheets for individual study, home practice or ordinary classroom teaching. The website does not certify grade-level readiness, guarantee alignment with a specific curriculum, or replace professional teaching judgment.</p>
  <h2>Check before distributing</h2>
  <p>Questions and answers are generated from mathematical rules, but they can still contain an error or be unsuitable for a particular learner. Review every worksheet and its answer key before handing it to students. In particular, printing physical measurement tools at anything other than Actual Size / 100% can make their dimensions inaccurate; check the printed calibration mark with a physical ruler.</p>
  <h2>Content and service limitations</h2>
  <p>The website and generated content are provided as available without a promise of uninterrupted service or guaranteed accuracy. Worksheet formats, available practice options and generators may change. A reproducible link records the generator version and settings; older links may not reproduce identical problems after a future upgrade.</p>
  <h2>No student records required</h2>
  <p>No account is necessary to use the worksheet generators. Please do not include student names, school identifiers or confidential information in any public feedback report. Read our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy policy</a> for information about local generation and hosting metadata.</p>
  <h2>Questions and corrections</h2>
  <p>For a suspected calculation mistake, print issue or accessibility problem, include the worksheet topic, settings, seed and generator version when contacting us. Do not share student information. See the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>
  <p><a href="/worksheets/">Browse the worksheet library</a></p>
 </article></div>
</Layout>
